{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453501-bond-famulus","id":1453501,"title":"Bond Famulus...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-25T18:35:25-07:00","id":1453501,"title":"Bond Famulus...","content":"Ok so... The power reads as follows:<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>&quot;Bond Famulus</b></u><br /> When Blood Bonding an animal, the vampire can make it a famulus, forming a mental link with it and facilitating the use of other Animalism powers. While this power alone does not allow two-way communication with the animal, it can follow simple verbal instructions such as \u201cstay\u201d and \u201ccome here.&quot; It attacks in defense of itself and its master but cannot otherwise be persuaded to fight something it would not normally attack.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Now.... can someone tell me exactly how this is NOT just bonding and ghouling a dog? Like what work is this &quot;mental link&quot; doin? Cause it seems like you still have to speak the commands... I mean hell... I'm just a guy and my dog does this for me with out a blood bond lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T19:07:15-07:00","id":1453504,"title":"","content":"It really does literally nothing by itself and only comes into play once you learn higher levels. Until then, it\u2019s power is that you can tell a Blood Bonded animal to sit and stay...which is pretty impressive if your animal is a cat or a bird or something other than a canine. My opinion, it is not a full Discipline power as wriitten. It should at least allow communication, like Animalism 1 has done for 30 years across all Masq and Req versions, but communication is now expressly and specifically not possible...although a &quot;mental link&quot; is established, but since it doesn't specify what that link entails, I guess it\u2019s just playing static until you get your lines installed with Animalism 2.<br /> <br /> I would argue for at least allowing normal Animalism 1 communication with your ghoul, or specifying the &quot;mental link&quot; conveys a sharing of emotions and senses (see through each others' eyes, etc) so you can at least strategize or gain intel, or even swapping levels with Bond Famulus and Feral Whispers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T19:14:13-07:00","id":1453505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453501-bond-famulus?p=1453504#post1453504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really does literally nothing by itself and only comes into play once you learn higher levels. Until then, it\u2019s power is that you can tell a Blood Bonded animal to sit and stay...which is pretty impressive if your animal is a cat or a bird or something other than a canine. My opinion, it is not a full Discipline power as wriitten. It should at least allow communication, like Animalism 1 has done for 30 years across all Masq and Req versions, but communication is now expressly and specifically not possible...although a &quot;mental link&quot; is established, but since it doesn't specify what that link entails, I guess it\u2019s just playing static until you get your lines installed with Animalism 2.<br /> <br /> I would argue for at least allowing normal Animalism 1 communication with your ghoul, or specifying the &quot;mental link&quot; conveys a sharing of emotions and senses (see through each others' eyes, etc) so you can at least strategize or gain intel, or even swapping levels with Bond Famulus and Feral Whispers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would agree, like at least some base line mental communication like a pseudodragon in D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T21:23:50-07:00","id":1453514,"title":"","content":"It allows you to have a ghoul without buying a retainer dot, and without spending enough blood to require a rouse check after it's done. It also effectively allows you to have 6 dots in Retainers eventually, since it doesn't cost a retainer dot. Even so, yeah, it's a little meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T02:12:49-07:00","id":1453527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453501-bond-famulus?p=1453514#post1453514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It allows you to have a ghoul without buying a retainer dot, and without spending enough blood to require a rouse check after it's done. It also effectively allows you to have 6 dots in Retainers eventually, since it doesn't cost a retainer dot. Even so, yeah, it's a little meh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, limiting how many animal ghouls you can keep to five dots (or even six) is frankly ridiculous, especially when dealing with small things like rats or birds. You should be able to ghoul however many critters you can get to drink your blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}